[h1]Arcane Ship Cores[/h1]

Arcane Cores is the official example content pack for the [b]Ship Core Framework[/b]. It provides [b]14 physical core profiles[/b] for combat ships, utility vessels, and stations.

A core defines the grid's role: size, mass, PCU, weapons, industry, speed, defenses, abilities, upgrades, ownership limits, and connector rules. These are specialized fleet roles rather than simple linear tiers.

[h2]Configuration Features[/h2]

[list]
[*]Minimum/maximum blocks, mass, and PCU
[*]Per-player, per-faction, faction-size, and faction-rank requirements
[*]Thruster, gyro, power, refinery, assembler, and drill modifiers
[*]Speed, boost, friction, passive defense, and active defense
[*]Power overclocking on selected profiles
[*]Weapon, industry, cargo, tool, and jump-drive limits
[*]Directional weapon and drill placement
[*]Allowed upgrade modules and backup-core counts
[*]Main-core priority and connector incompatibilities
[/list]

[h2]Recent Framework Support[/h2]

[list]
[*]Build-preview arrows show permitted block directions
[*]Backup cores must match the active main core's exact orientation
[*]Selected cores can overclock power output at the cost of reactor damage and cooldown
[*]Upgrade modules modify performance, defense, abilities, and limits
[*]Active defense and speed boosts use profile-specific durations and cooldowns
[*]Minimum-size and ownership rules prevent class abuse
[/list]

[h1]Combat Grids[/h1]

[b]Interceptor[/b] - Fastest light craft; mobility and fixed-forward weapons.
[b]Fighter[/b] - Forward-strike craft with heavier weapon options.
[b]Gunship[/b] - Armed small-grid support with turrets and power overclocking.
[b]Frigate[/b] - Fast frontline brawler with point defense and active defenses.
[b]Destroyer[/b] - Long-range heavy-weapon specialist.
[b]Cruiser[/b] - Flexible fleet backbone with combat, limited industry, and overclocking.
[b]Battleship[/b] - Faction capital ship built around heavy broadside firepower.

[h1]Utility Grids[/h1]

[b]Courier[/b] - Fast cargo and jump-capable logistics vessel.
[b]Utility[/b] - General construction, repair, mining, and industry ship.
[b]Extractor[/b] - Dedicated miner/refiner with directional drills and overclocking.
[b]Harvester[/b] - Faction-scale industrial mining vessel with high drill and refinery capacity.

[h1]Stations[/h1]

[b]Outpost[/b] - Compact remote infrastructure and defense platform.
[b]Stronghold[/b] - Fortified forward base with industry, safe-zone support, and overclocking.
[b]Citadel[/b] - Founder-gated faction headquarters with maximum industry, defense, and backup capacity.

[h2]Upgrade Modules[/h2]

Large- and small-grid modules are limited per profile:

[list]
[*][b]Combat[/b] - More weapons and defense at an efficiency/speed cost
[*][b]Economy[/b] - Better production, refining, power, and efficiency
[*][b]Handling[/b] - Better thrust, gyros, speed, and boost
[*][b]Harvester[/b] - Better drilling/refining and additional drill capacity
[*][b]Overdrive[/b] - More thrust, speed, boost, and power at an efficiency/durability cost
[/list]

[h2]Using a Core[/h2]

Build a core on the grid to select its profile. The first valid core becomes main. Allowed backup cores must face in exactly the same forward/up orientation.

Use [b]/core help[/b] for commands and [b]/core limits[/b] while looking at a grid. Limits are also available through the build-preview HUD and Core Status LCD.

